1
00:00:07,650 --> 00:00:11,170
 If the 16th century could be called the Century of Exploring New Continents,

2
00:00:11,270 --> 00:00:13,130
 the 17th would be that of colonization.

3
00:00:14,110 --> 00:00:15,850
 But let's go back to the beginning.

4
00:00:15,850 --> 00:00:19,690
 In 1579, Sir Francis Drake landed in North America

5
00:00:19,690 --> 00:00:22,870
 and claimed it in the name of Queen Elizabeth of England.

6
00:00:25,420 --> 00:00:26,700
 Sailor, just a minute there.

7
00:00:26,880 --> 00:00:28,280
 You're forgetting Her Majesty's picture.

8
00:00:28,420 --> 00:00:28,560
 Eh?

9
00:00:28,700 --> 00:00:31,880
 How am I supposed to put up a picture?

10
00:00:32,100 --> 00:00:32,840
 I haven't got one.

11
00:00:33,330 --> 00:00:33,710
 Hmm.

12
00:00:35,760 --> 00:00:37,100
 Here.

13
00:00:42,350 --> 00:00:49,020
 On Oak Island in North Carolina,

14
00:00:49,140 --> 00:00:52,060
 an expedition has just arrived, commanded by Sir Walter Raleigh.

15
00:00:54,320 --> 00:00:57,050
 Gee, strange men are coming.

16
00:00:57,070 --> 00:01:02,480
 ashore i swear it they're there they came in big wooden houses on the water what are we supposed to

17
00:01:02,480 --> 00:01:12,370
 do we better go kill them oh we keep calm it's possible they came in peace let us wait there's

18
00:01:12,370 --> 00:01:17,810
 nobody about we looked everything's peace and quiet sir john good we'll settle right here

19
00:01:17,810 --> 00:01:55,180
 down in history virginia dare the first child born in the new england colony sir john white's

20
00:01:55,180 --> 00:02:00,490
 colony mysteriously disappeared for 12 years they searched for survivors but in vain

21
00:02:00,490 --> 00:02:02,110
 They had vanished.

22
00:02:03,060 --> 00:02:06,800
 A strange new plant was brought back to England and was causing a sensation.

23
00:02:07,650 --> 00:02:10,400
 Careful, mister. Your toothpick, it's on fire.

24
00:02:14,880 --> 00:02:21,740
 Toothpick. Tobacco. It's all the rage now.

25
00:02:25,870 --> 00:02:32,880
 But, uh, you're all right. You're not sick.

26
00:02:34,610 --> 00:02:37,590
 Toothpick. Chewing tobacco. It's all the rage.

27
00:02:37,890 --> 00:02:51,390
 Sir, you have a terrible cold.

28
00:02:51,660 --> 00:02:56,940
 Not a bit of it, but I'm taking snuff. It's all the rage these days.

29
00:02:56,940 --> 00:03:06,160
 It's ugly to look at. Its odor is disgusting. It rots the brine and ruins the lungs.

30
00:03:06,380 --> 00:03:14,380
 Nevertheless, 20,000 pounds were shipped from America in 1618 and 500,000 pounds, 25 times more, 10 years later.

31
00:03:14,580 --> 00:03:19,250
 And 200 million pounds, a thousand times more, 50 years later.

32
00:03:19,810 --> 00:03:21,850
 As they said, it was all the rage.

33
00:03:41,760 --> 00:04:02,490
 Smith, congratulations.

34
00:04:02,760 --> 00:04:05,480
 Here in Chesapeake Bay, you found a splendid place to settle.

35
00:04:05,640 --> 00:04:09,360
 Yes, and we should name our colony Jamestown in honor of our sovereign.

36
00:04:10,020 --> 00:04:11,930
 Tell me, what do you think?

37
00:04:11,930 --> 00:04:46,340
 Do you suppose you gentlemen could help us put up some strong cabins so we can get through the winter?

38
00:04:46,480 --> 00:04:51,780
 We are in the upper class, and we don't soil our hands doing mean your labor.

39
00:04:51,980 --> 00:04:54,020
 You, my man, are made for hard work.

40
00:04:54,530 --> 00:04:54,860
 Sir?

41
00:05:19,060 --> 00:05:46,170
 Members of the colony, only 32 survive the first winter.

42
00:05:47,230 --> 00:05:49,680
 I think the harvest will be a good one.

43
00:05:50,630 --> 00:05:53,050
 So, let's go over and see how the tobacco's doing.

44
00:05:53,600 --> 00:05:54,180
 Let's go.

45
00:05:57,090 --> 00:06:04,380
 The presiding head of the colony, I declare that anyone who doesn't work, doesn't eat.

46
00:06:10,620 --> 00:06:14,720
 Again, their fields are bigger, they take more of our land.

47
00:06:15,040 --> 00:06:17,160
 Settlers speak with forked tongue, we kill them.

48
00:06:17,720 --> 00:06:18,480
 This way.

49
00:06:31,460 --> 00:06:37,400
 One smith, chief of colony, does not keep his word.

50
00:06:37,400 --> 00:06:42,290
 You and your people once more take from us.

51
00:06:42,870 --> 00:06:43,730
 We trust no more.

52
00:06:43,850 --> 00:06:45,410
 You, Captain Smith, you will die.

53
00:06:45,650 --> 00:06:47,250
 You will be a lesson to your people.

54
00:06:47,490 --> 00:06:48,730
 Great Chief Powhatan has spoken.

55
00:06:48,830 --> 00:06:49,370
 No, you can't. It isn't right.

56
00:06:49,530 --> 00:06:50,770
 I insist. I...

57
00:06:50,770 --> 00:07:02,840
 Me, Pocahontas, your own daughter.

58
00:07:02,960 --> 00:07:04,540
 I beg your mercy to pardon him.

59
00:07:06,370 --> 00:07:08,780
 An impossible request to my daughter.

60
00:07:08,880 --> 00:07:10,380
 The man has betrayed our confidence.

61
00:07:10,580 --> 00:07:11,280
 He must be put to death.

62
00:07:11,300 --> 00:07:12,500
 Then you must kill me as well.

63
00:07:15,210 --> 00:07:18,590
 Will you guarantee cheating will stop?

64
00:07:18,850 --> 00:07:20,190
 He will keep his word.

65
00:07:21,090 --> 00:07:24,510
 With my life, I swear he will, Great Powhatan.

66
00:07:24,890 --> 00:07:26,580
 Then so be it. You can let him go.

67
00:07:26,580 --> 00:08:09,310
 Father, I do, my dear.

68
00:08:09,500 --> 00:08:11,740
 Yes, indeed. These good men are able to pay.

69
00:08:12,880 --> 00:08:16,790
 30 pounds of tobacco surely isn't too high a price to pay for a charming girl.

70
00:08:16,950 --> 00:08:17,050
 No!

71
00:08:27,360 --> 00:08:38,370
 Slaves arrive in Virginia. This was the beginning of slavery in America.

72
00:08:42,560 --> 00:08:47,530
 You see, children, stupidity and intolerance have always existed and in all religions.

73
00:08:48,280 --> 00:08:56,360
 In 1581, the Protestant Queen Elizabeth of England decreed that anyone who didn't attend church on Sunday would be fined 20 pounds sterling.

74
00:08:56,700 --> 00:08:58,340
 Was that a lot of money then?

75
00:08:58,340 --> 00:09:02,540
 Oh, yes, it was, and anyone who converted to Catholicism was sentenced to be executed.

76
00:09:02,900 --> 00:09:06,640
 Jesuits who wanted to remain in this beautiful land were hanged and drawn,

77
00:09:06,960 --> 00:09:09,690
 taken down, and their entrails disemboweled.

78
00:09:12,620 --> 00:09:15,680
 That 147 of them died in this way.

79
00:09:17,430 --> 00:09:20,330
 Now, 20,000 pilgrims who disagreed with this,

80
00:09:20,560 --> 00:09:23,160
 this notion of divine mercy emigrated to Holland.

81
00:09:23,640 --> 00:09:27,810
 I would like to read this document, which is named for our ship, the Mayflower.

82
00:09:29,650 --> 00:09:34,690
 Glory of God and the propagation of the Christian faith,

83
00:09:34,690 --> 00:09:39,400
 We have undertaken to found a new colony in the north of Virginia.

84
00:09:40,760 --> 00:09:46,340
 In the presence of one and all, we agree to unite in one political unity for the good of the colony.

85
00:09:46,740 --> 00:09:48,680
 I want you now to come here and sign it.

86
00:09:52,310 --> 00:09:57,300
 First, our leader will sign Captain Bradford.

87
00:09:58,030 --> 00:10:03,760
 Then, Captain Lionel Standish, you will be responsible for our safety.

88
00:10:06,400 --> 00:10:10,530
 Say, Captain, wouldn't you say we have drifted somewhat?

89
00:10:10,790 --> 00:10:13,550
 I think you're right. We're much too far north, Captain.

90
00:10:13,740 --> 00:10:15,590
 We're probably off New England.

91
00:10:15,590 --> 00:10:34,290
 It's ideal for our settlement.

92
00:10:37,710 --> 00:10:46,750
 It was a harsh winter, and once again, over half the colony perished.

93
00:10:47,690 --> 00:10:50,770
 Meanwhile, relations with the Indians became friendly.

94
00:10:52,260 --> 00:10:55,620
 I put fish into the land so Corden would be strong and grow.

95
00:10:55,890 --> 00:10:58,580
 You're a friend, Squanto. Everyone thanks you.

96
00:11:00,190 --> 00:11:04,320
 Give me your furs, and I'll give you my shovel, all right?

97
00:11:06,080 --> 00:11:13,730
 Well, what do you think of our little town of Plymouth?

98
00:11:13,830 --> 00:11:16,090
 Wouldn't you say she's beginning to look very, very good?

99
00:11:16,090 --> 00:11:20,830
 Well, I'm happy now that we have comfortable houses and plenty of food to see us through the winter.

100
00:11:21,190 --> 00:11:23,790
 Uh, Captain Bradford, you come...

101
00:11:23,790 --> 00:11:24,960
 Why?

102
00:11:25,080 --> 00:11:25,720
 Well, I have an idea.

103
00:11:25,820 --> 00:11:28,980
 Why don't we have a great feast to thank the good Lord?

104
00:11:29,550 --> 00:11:32,120
 We might name it Thanksgiving Day.

105
00:11:32,480 --> 00:11:36,240
 Yes, and we'll hold races, and we'll have roast turkey with cranberry sauce, and with...

106
00:11:36,240 --> 00:11:39,880
 Just a minute, we said the feast was to thank the Lord for his blessings.

107
00:11:42,030 --> 00:11:44,850
 Forgive them, Lord, they know not what they do.

108
00:11:45,370 --> 00:11:48,010
 After all, they are your children, and they deserve a good time.

109
00:12:02,480 --> 00:12:24,510
 These are your children.

110
00:12:25,280 --> 00:12:37,770
 They have suffered deprivations, pleasures of the table, partake in these shrivelous pursuits each November.

111
00:12:37,990 --> 00:12:39,820
 Is it really so much to ask?

112
00:12:41,200 --> 00:12:47,940
 Great Pilgrim's Festival lasted three days and now every November Americans celebrate Thanksgiving Day.

113
00:13:00,980 --> 00:13:06,540
 To a place called Massa-what? Massa, Massa, Massa-fish. No, Massa, the Massa-choose-sets.

114
00:13:06,750 --> 00:13:20,580
 Never heard of a place on my ship.

115
00:13:21,060 --> 00:13:24,000
 Realize, my son, they too need milk for their babies.

116
00:13:26,090 --> 00:13:29,730
 My son, they need goat cheese. So, goats?

117
00:13:30,030 --> 00:13:37,110
 I know, my son, they need pigs and chickens for their hungry children.

118
00:13:37,290 --> 00:13:39,110
 Why not some tigers and a few elephants?

119
00:13:39,510 --> 00:13:40,730
 Hey, hey, where are you going?

120
00:13:40,730 --> 00:14:09,530
 Thirty-seven ships arrive in New England.

121
00:14:10,660 --> 00:14:13,250
 In the following years, a great migration took place.

122
00:14:13,370 --> 00:14:16,230
 Over 200 ships and 20,000 colonists.

123
00:14:16,590 --> 00:14:19,090
 They're all sorts of people with differing opinions.

124
00:14:19,860 --> 00:14:21,160
 I am the Reverend Colton.

125
00:14:21,240 --> 00:14:24,480
 I am here to tell you democracy is a false doctrine and aberration.

126
00:14:25,230 --> 00:14:30,720
 It is beyond belief that God ever intended this form of government for church or for state.

127
00:14:30,720 --> 00:14:32,060
 I am Thomas Hooker.

128
00:14:32,280 --> 00:14:33,340
 I believe in democracy.

129
00:14:33,520 --> 00:14:35,380
 The source of all authority is the people.

130
00:14:35,660 --> 00:14:39,440
 And since we are not allowed to live democratically here, we will go elsewhere.

131
00:14:40,740 --> 00:14:42,710
 Those who are with me, follow this way.

132
00:14:43,880 --> 00:14:46,900
 Hooker went south where he founded the state of Connecticut.

133
00:14:47,690 --> 00:14:50,770
 Here in Salem, we will forever follow the footsteps of the first pilgrims.

134
00:14:50,850 --> 00:14:53,110
 Here we will, every one of us, do as we wish in freedom.

135
00:14:53,390 --> 00:14:55,920
 I, John Endicott, tell you this, and so hearken.

136
00:14:56,290 --> 00:15:00,380
 I, Roger Williams, maintain that no power, monarch, or parliament, or government

137
00:15:00,380 --> 00:15:03,450
 shall have greater authority than that granted by the people.

138
00:15:03,550 --> 00:15:07,240
 We should buy Indian lands, pay for it legally, never steal it,

139
00:15:07,280 --> 00:15:10,780
 Because in the eyes of the Lord, an Indian soul is just as one of ours.

140
00:15:12,040 --> 00:15:14,910
 Later, Roger Williams founded Providence and Rhode Island.

141
00:15:15,140 --> 00:15:17,520
 The Holy Spirit spoke to me last night in my sleep.

142
00:15:17,560 --> 00:15:21,600
 I say that we have no need of clergymen, for each of us has a spirit that will guide us.

143
00:15:21,820 --> 00:15:23,240
 Yes, our inner light of truth.

144
00:15:24,220 --> 00:15:26,990
 Yes, our brother has just spoken with great wisdom.

145
00:15:27,330 --> 00:15:29,690
 The Quakers are banned in Boston and leave the city.

146
00:15:29,810 --> 00:15:31,670
 John Wheelwright is condemned as a heretic.

147
00:15:31,910 --> 00:15:33,330
 To the north he founds New Hampshire.

148
00:15:33,330 --> 00:15:36,270
 We have no need for an organized church.

149
00:15:36,590 --> 00:15:39,710
 God can talk to us directly so long as we feel the presence of God within us.

150
00:15:39,710 --> 00:15:44,550
 Ann Hutchinson, your words are sacrilegious. You are hereby condemned of heresy and banished forever.

151
00:15:44,990 --> 00:15:48,490
 Ann Hutchinson, with her 14 children, settled in Rhode Island.

152
00:15:49,640 --> 00:15:53,000
 Other colonists were to be banished for less noble reasons.

153
00:16:09,640 --> 00:16:10,960
 Is he here with his men?

154
00:16:11,760 --> 00:16:14,900
 Right? Miles and his men? They'll see what I'm made of.

155
00:16:16,790 --> 00:16:18,660
 Yes, Chief, not so much powder. Stop.

156
00:16:18,940 --> 00:16:20,840
 That's too much. Anything could happen.

157
00:16:20,840 --> 00:16:25,120
 No, I put in just enough to blow Miles Dennis to kingdom come in the door.

158
00:16:25,610 --> 00:16:27,330
 Open up the door.

159
00:16:30,310 --> 00:17:01,590
 During the first half of the 17th century, immigrant colonists from England all came and colonized.

160
00:17:02,090 --> 00:17:07,610
 Virginia, Massachusetts, Connecticut, New Hampshire, and Rhode Island.

161
00:17:08,020 --> 00:17:12,330
 And a group of 300 Catholics came and founded Maryland.

162
00:17:13,530 --> 00:17:17,790
 Thus, the English held a significant portion of the American eastern seaboard.

163
00:17:18,230 --> 00:17:19,030
 But not all.

164
00:17:19,400 --> 00:17:21,780
 The Dutch had settled in New York.

165
00:17:21,780 --> 00:17:25,370
 I mean, in New Amsterdam.

166
00:17:46,570 --> 00:17:57,300
 Right here, your lands are over there.

167
00:17:57,310 --> 00:18:03,070
 Agree this is our land here.

168
00:18:03,070 --> 00:18:05,560
 No, our lands and they're keeping them.

169
00:18:05,560 --> 00:18:07,580
 No, our lands and we keep them.

170
00:18:07,580 --> 00:18:09,890
 I'm going to tell you one more time.

171
00:18:09,890 --> 00:18:11,970
 Our lands, we won't keep them up.

172
00:18:11,970 --> 00:18:14,280
 We're going to keep our own land.

173
00:18:14,280 --> 00:18:16,090
 It always belonged to us, white man.

174
00:18:16,090 --> 00:18:21,510
 I thought we agreed to know why white man stands on my left foot.

175
00:18:21,510 --> 00:18:24,750
 And why is red man standing on white man's left foot?

176
00:18:24,750 --> 00:18:28,280
 You are crushing red man's foot standing on land of his ancestors.

177
00:18:28,280 --> 00:18:31,810
 Red man is crushing foot of white man standing on his own land.

178
00:18:31,810 --> 00:18:47,330
 What's going on here?

179
00:18:47,330 --> 00:18:50,620
 Just who are you?

180
00:18:50,620 --> 00:18:55,130
 Minwit, Peter Minwit, the new governor of this colony.

181
00:18:55,130 --> 00:18:57,420
 Declanusland is there!

182
00:18:57,420 --> 00:19:04,550
 Calm down, please. To kiss between us, I'm willing to pay. I'll buy your land.

183
00:19:04,550 --> 00:19:06,550
 In fact, the whole island.

184
00:19:06,550 --> 00:19:09,950
 And I'm going to pay with something you've never seen.

185
00:19:09,950 --> 00:19:14,030
 Admit, that is really extraordinary.

186
00:19:14,030 --> 00:19:35,040
 I'll give you all these wonderful trickets for your old Manhattan.

187
00:19:35,040 --> 00:19:37,760
 It's a pretty good deal.

188
00:19:37,760 --> 00:19:41,590
 Well, you take my word. They're worth $24 at today's prices.

189
00:19:41,590 --> 00:19:47,090
 And that was that. The island of Manhattan was bought for $24 worth of junk jewelry.

190
00:19:48,060 --> 00:19:50,160
 New Amsterdam prospered and grew.

191
00:19:51,630 --> 00:19:55,930
 There's the wall that became Wall Street, and one day in 1664...

192
00:19:55,930 --> 00:19:59,360
 Governor! Governor Stuyvesant! Quickly, come and see!

193
00:20:00,350 --> 00:20:03,080
 What is it? What is all this racket about?

194
00:20:03,140 --> 00:20:06,880
 It's the British Navy's scum, sir!

195
00:20:07,190 --> 00:20:09,930
 Are you sure the British Navy will go and see about this?

196
00:20:11,260 --> 00:20:25,420
 What are you doing in New Amsterdam? I'm ordering you in your nutshells to go.

197
00:20:25,420 --> 00:20:29,300
 May I just point out that we are at war, but surrendering will treat you well, well?

198
00:20:29,490 --> 00:20:32,400
 Are you crazy or what? We'll fight until we're dead.

199
00:20:32,660 --> 00:20:33,060
 Sir?

200
00:20:36,240 --> 00:20:43,160
 Gunpowder, what are you waiting for? Bring the powder.

201
00:20:45,980 --> 00:20:50,700
 It will, and blow those nutshells out of the water.

202
00:20:51,320 --> 00:20:53,980
 Can't obey those orders for a couple of days.

203
00:20:54,760 --> 00:20:55,770
 What? Why?

204
00:20:55,990 --> 00:20:58,210
 It'll take a couple of days to dry the powder out.

205
00:20:58,410 --> 00:20:59,710
 Have to surrender, surrender.

206
00:21:00,470 --> 00:21:03,570
 Accept your surrender, Mr. Stuyvesant. From now on, this is New York.

207
00:21:04,050 --> 00:21:13,610
 And along with New York came New Jersey.

208
00:21:13,610 --> 00:21:16,610
 He followed by Delaware, the ninth English colony.

209
00:21:17,520 --> 00:21:23,160
 Meanwhile, back in London...

210
00:21:23,160 --> 00:21:28,090
 Quiet, my friends. Let's permit Anthony Cooper to explain his plan.

211
00:21:28,670 --> 00:21:34,060
 As you know, John Locke, the philosopher, was helpful to us in propounding the various constitutions for the new colonies.

212
00:21:34,730 --> 00:21:35,550
 We quite show him.

213
00:21:35,550 --> 00:21:43,360
 Our colony of Carolina will belong to the landed gentry at first.

214
00:21:43,720 --> 00:21:45,700
 Naturally, that means the present company.

215
00:21:46,060 --> 00:21:50,020
 Then there will be land gravenes who will hold 15,000 hectares each.

216
00:21:50,020 --> 00:21:54,560
 than khakis who will be awarded a thousand, the commoners, however, and the servants will

217
00:21:54,560 --> 00:22:00,900
 have nothing. And as for the slaves, yes, well, that's another matter. They are to be

218
00:22:00,900 --> 00:22:11,620
 given the right to work our lands for no payment whatever. The landowners will appoint a governor

219
00:22:11,620 --> 00:22:30,720
 from among their... Oh. Land graves and cassocks, rights of white men, rights of black men.

220
00:22:30,720 --> 00:22:35,440
 What's it all mean? It's all absurd. Go on, teach them field workers not to be so

221
00:22:35,440 --> 00:22:36,700
 Please, it has work to do.

222
00:22:38,590 --> 00:22:42,670
 My son William would like to go to America, sire.

223
00:22:43,050 --> 00:22:45,060
 Your Majesty, he's rather a poet.

224
00:22:45,570 --> 00:22:47,770
 And since Your Majesty feels indebted to us,

225
00:22:47,770 --> 00:22:53,280
 I wonder if Your Majesty would consider granting lands in the New World to him

226
00:22:53,280 --> 00:22:55,400
 to hold in perpetuity, sire.

227
00:22:56,480 --> 00:23:00,250
 Penn, old chap, you know I can refuse you nothing.

228
00:23:01,170 --> 00:23:03,590
 There are unexplored areas in northern Maryland.

229
00:23:03,890 --> 00:23:05,470
 Take them, young man. They are yours.

230
00:23:06,080 --> 00:23:08,680
 Thank you, Your Majesty. I'll call them Pennsylvania.

231
00:23:10,090 --> 00:23:14,940
 Yes, Majesty, it's because of the many fours that are there.

232
00:23:26,490 --> 00:23:45,720
 Queen's great chief, we want to establish on this land a just and peaceful society.

233
00:23:46,160 --> 00:23:49,310
 To do this, we will sign a peace treaty of perpetual brotherhood.

234
00:23:50,960 --> 00:23:53,400
 No one will ever be persecuted for his beliefs.

235
00:23:54,280 --> 00:23:57,100
 Only murder and treason will be punishable by death.

236
00:23:58,530 --> 00:24:02,930
 In England, you see, people were being hanged for almost no reason at all.

237
00:24:03,290 --> 00:24:06,150
 These liberal laws would attract many immigrants.

238
00:24:07,010 --> 00:24:10,130
 Philadelphia, the city of brotherly love, became a great capital.

239
00:24:10,130 --> 00:24:19,430
 9 states plus the two Carolinas, that makes 11, and Pennsylvania makes a dozen.

240
00:24:19,430 --> 00:24:23,650
 Wait 12, but there were 13. Where is that 13th original colony?

241
00:24:23,650 --> 00:24:30,550
 I have to wait a while. More than 100 years and a lot of tribulation before the 13th was settled.

242
00:24:30,550 --> 00:24:45,700
 Undercoming Dakota represent his prestigious Majesty George III of England. Proclaim Olgin!

243
00:24:45,700 --> 00:24:54,770
 General James Oglethorpe declared that people should be sent soon to populate northern Florida

244
00:24:54,770 --> 00:24:56,890
 Florida before the Spanish get it!

245
00:24:56,890 --> 00:25:03,780
 The colony of Georgia in honor of our King George III!

246
00:25:03,780 --> 00:25:06,740
 And there we are, the 13th colony.

247
00:25:06,740 --> 00:25:10,710
 Explorers are now followed by settlers who will clear the land for crops

248
00:25:10,710 --> 00:25:13,120
 and create a fascinating country.

